# RELEASE-AGE QUARANTINE (audit "Add a 14-day release-age quarantine for uv and
# npm", part of #60), the npm counterpart of [tool.uv] exclude-newer in the root
# pyproject.toml. npm resolves a dependency (`npm install`, `npm update`,
# `npm audit fix`) only to versions published at least 14 days ago, a rolling
# window counted from each run's clock: a hijacked release that is unpublished
# within days never reaches package-lock.json. `npm ci`, which CI runs, installs
# the lockfile as written and is unaffected.
# min-release-age is a number of days and needs an npm that knows it: the npm
# of Node 24.22 (11.19.1) documents it; an npm without it warns "Unknown project
# config" and ignores the line. To take a fix younger than the window, name the
# package in min-release-age-exclude, never a shorter window.
# tests/unit/scripts/test_release_age_quarantine.py holds this line present.
min-release-age=14
